 ◆ Done. No schema change was needed, and no new dependencies were added.
 ▎ 
 ▎ ▌ Final report
 ▎ 
 ▎ A1 — Capacity: already true (verified), not changed.
 ▎ booking-creation.repository.ts:100-108 reserves a tier with a conditional UPDATE "TicketType" SET "soldCount" = "soldCount" + ${totalQty} WHERE "ticketTypeId" = ${ticketTypeId} AND
 ▎ "soldCount" + ${totalQty} <= "quantity" inside prisma.$transaction — the guard is in the SQL, not a read-then-write. Proven by apps/server/tests/checkout-capacity.spec.ts:98 ("25
 ▎ concurrent claims for one last seat let exactly one through") and :123.
 ▎ cd apps/server && npx playwright test tests/checkout-capacity.spec.ts → 7 passed.
 ▎ 
 ▎ A2 — Hold expiry: changed. HOLD_TTL_SECONDS now comes from config (apps/server/src/config/index.ts:104-111, default 600, invalid values fall back to 600). It replaces four
 ▎ hardcoded copies: booking-lifecycle.service.ts:20 (HOLD_DURATION_MS), slot.service.ts:41, slot-walk-in.service.ts:23, lib/cache/slot.ts:17. The existing worker does the
 ▎ expiry (index.worker.ts sweep + booking-expiry.worker.ts), no new service. Idempotency proven by checkout-capacity.spec.ts:247 (two concurrent releaseHoldTx → exactly one
 ▎ wins, capacity returned once).

 ▎ A3 — Late payment: changed. forcePaidAfterRaceTx previously incremented soldCount uncapped — a late capture could oversell the event. It now re-claims capacity with the
 ▎ same conditional update inside the transaction (booking-lifecycle.repository.ts:333-347) and throws CapacityNotAvailableError when the seat was resold. The finalizer catches that
 ▎ and refunds through the existing Razorpay client (booking-payment-finalizer.service.ts:527-604, refundLateCapture), falling back to flagForReconciliation if the refund call
 ▎ fails. Proven by checkout-capacity.spec.ts:158 (seat free → confirmed, soldCount 1) and :180 (seat resold → rejects, soldCount stays 1, booking not PAID).

 ▎ A4 — Exactly once: changed. The webhook's existingPayment.status === "COMPLETED" early-return skipped every retry, so a delivery that crashed after marking the payment but
 ▎ before confirming the booking stranded the buyer. It now skips only when the booking is also settled (payment-webhook.service.ts:617-643). The exactly-once gate is the atomic
 ▎ markPaidTx status transition, proven by checkout-capacity.spec.ts:212 and :231; duplicate-event dedupe proven by checkout-integrity.spec.ts:56 plus the existing webhook-
 ▎ dedup.spec.ts.

 ▎ A5 — Money: already true (verified). POST /bookings/:id/payment-order takes only bookingId — no price from the client. The order amount comes from the DB booking
 ▎ total via toPaise (booking-payment.service.ts:138), integer paise, and toPaise is the repo's single rounding point. I only swapped Math.round(booking.total * 100) →
 ▎ toPaise(booking.total) (same value, one helper). Proven by checkout-integrity.spec.ts:36-52.

 ▎ W1 — Web payment step: changed. PaymentStep.tsx had no countdown and opened Razorpay without checking expiry. It now renders the existing HoldCountdown (which derives time
